* 4x4 Resistive Crossbar 
* Row voltages are inputs, column currents are outputs
*M = 
*1  2  3  4
*2  3  4  1
*3  4  1  2
*4  1  2  3

* Input voltage sources (rows)
V1 row1 0 DC 1V
V2 row2 0 DC 2V
V3 row3 0 DC 3V
V4 row4 0 DC 4V

* Crossbar resistors (row, col intersections)
*the conductance (G = 1/R) at each intersection.
*but I scaled up by 10k to keep resistances reasonable
*therefor R = 10k/M
R11 row1 col1 10k
R12 row1 col2 5k
R13 row1 col3 {10000/3}
R14 row1 col4 2.5k
R21 row2 col1 5k
R22 row2 col2 {10000/3}
R23 row2 col3 2.5k
R24 row2 col4 10k
R31 row3 col1 {10000/3}
R32 row3 col2 2.5k
R33 row3 col3 10k
R34 row3 col4 5k
R41 row4 col1 2.5k
R42 row4 col2 10k
R43 row4 col3 5k
R44 row4 col4 {10000/3}

* Column nodes need to be grounded to measure current
Vout1 col1 0 DC 0V
Vout2 col2 0 DC 0V
Vout3 col3 0 DC 0V
Vout4 col4 0 DC 0V

* Measure current through the grounding sources
.PRINT DC I(Vout1) I(Vout2) I(Vout3) I(Vout4)
.DC V1 1 1 1
.END